+    statementEn: "Two expressions [$D_1(x)$ and $D_2(x)$] involving delta functions are said to be equal if\n$$\\int_{-\\infty}^{+\\infty} f(x) D_1(x) dx = \\int_{-\\infty}^{+\\infty} f(x) D_2(x) dx,$$\nfor any (ordinary) function $f(x)$.\n(a) Show that\n$$\\delta(cx) = \\frac{1}{|c|}\\delta(x), \\tag{2.124}$$\nwhere $c$ is a real constant.\n(b) Let $\\theta(x)$ be the **step function**:\n$$\\theta(x) \\equiv \\begin{cases} 1, & \\text{if } x > 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if } x < 0. \\end{cases} \\tag{2.125}$$\n[In the rare case where it actually matters, we define $\\theta(0)$ to be 1/2.] Show that $d\\theta/dx = \\delta(x)$.",
+    statementEs: "Se dice que dos expresiones [$D_1(x)$ y $D_2(x)$] que involucran deltas son iguales si\n$$\\int_{-\\infty}^{+\\infty} f(x)D_1(x)\\, dx = \\int_{-\\infty}^{+\\infty} f(x)D_2(x)\\, dx,$$\npara cualquier función (ordinaria) $f(x)$.\n(a) Muestra que\n$$\\delta(cx) = \\frac{1}{|c|}\\delta(x), \\tag{2.124}$$\ndonde $c$ es una constante real.\n(b) Sea $\\theta(x)$ la **función escalón**:\n$$\\theta(x) \\equiv \\begin{cases} 1, & \\text{si } x > 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{si } x < 0. \\end{cases} \\tag{2.125}$$\n[En el raro caso en que de verdad importe, definimos $\\theta(0) = 1/2$.] Muestra que $d\\theta/dx = \\delta(x)$.",
